<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio nigrofasciatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 27 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), Pass 2 — Morphological realism / specimen match: 83/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Side-by-side, the Parichy fish (eye, fins, caption, scale bar) is preserved and the trunk carries the cellular melanophore field. The chronoseries strip separates margaritatus spots, nigrofasciatus broken stripes, and rerio continuous stripes. The trunk field is a fine dash pattern, not a repaint of the three broad body stripes, which is the right object at 27 µm and a limit on silhouette match." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
