<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Danio nigrofasciatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 27 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), Pass 2 (Danio nigrofasciatus)",
        "Danio nigrofasciatus Schnakenberg wavelength at 27 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), Pass 2 faithfully reproduces Danio nigrofasciatus morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio nigrofasciatus specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Danio nigrofasciatus" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a fit to the photograph's dorsoventral darkness profile (Pearson r = 0.023).",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim more than one specimen, and does not claim a second assessor.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the organ-scale ~1 mm stripe spacing of slot 1203.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Alpha sweep, ablation, KS, and anterior-posterior holdout.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Chronoseries alphas 1.05, 6/1.15, and 8.5 at geological age 0 Ma.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Explicit-Euler anisotropic Schnakenberg with dx chosen so analytical lambda_c = 2.71e-05 m.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Trunk composite on the SHA-pinned Parichy photograph and a 12-frame growth GIF.",
        "reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. 2009: Danio pigment cells implement short-range activation and long-range inhibition and can form stripes or spots.",
        "reported_in_source: Parichy 2006: D. nigrofasciatus keeps a striped dorsum and a broken ventral field, unlike spotted D. margaritatus and striped D. rerio.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the critical-wavenumber formula.",
        "reported_in_source: Volkening and Sandstede 2018 and Podobnik et al. 2020: iridophores and Kcnj13 change Danio pattern symmetry.",
        "transfer_boundary: 27 µm is imposed by dx from the catalog cellular tier. The whole-body photograph does not resolve 27 µm.",
        "transfer_boundary: alpha is a stand-in for iridophore and Kcnj13 coupling, not a fitted channel conductance." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Danio nigrofasciatus (Holocene (Extant))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Danio" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-nigrofasciatus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/danio_nigrofasciatus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Danio nigrofasciatus; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the critical-wavenumber formula. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Nakamasu et al. 2009: Danio pigment cells implement short-range activation and long-range inhibition and can form stripes or spots. | Parichy 2006: D. nigrofasciatus keeps a striped dorsum and a broken ventral field, unlike spotted D. margaritatus and striped D. rerio. | Volkening and Sandstede 2018 and Podobnik et al. 2020: iridophores and Kcnj13 change Danio pattern symmetry.; reconstructed_in_script: Explicit-Euler anisotropic Schnakenberg with dx chosen so analytical lambda_c = 2.71e-05 m. | Chronoseries alphas 1.05, 6/1.15, and 8.5 at geological age 0 Ma. | Alpha sweep, ablation, KS, and anterior-posterior holdout. | Trunk composite on the SHA-pinned Parichy photograph and a 12-frame growth GIF.; transfer_boundary: 27 µm is imposed by dx from the catalog cellular tier. The whole-body photograph does not resolve 27 µm. | alpha is a stand-in for iridophore and Kcnj13 coupling, not a fitted channel conductance.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the organ-scale ~1 mm stripe spacing of slot 1203. | Does not claim a fit to the photograph's dorsoventral darkness profile (Pearson r = 0.023). | Does not claim more than one specimen, and does not claim a second assessor.]; phenomenon_size: 20 µm (2.018e-05 m, log10=-4.695 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 20 µm to 4.5 cm): 20 µm:danio-aesculapii-bioelectric-polarity, 63 µm:danio-aesculapii-vertex-packing, 1.0 mm:danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength, 2.0 mm:danio-aesculapii-clock-wavefront, 4.5 mm:danio-aesculapii-morphogen-condensation, 5.5 mm:danio-aesculapii-elastic-buckling, 6.3 mm:danio-aesculapii-flux-canalization, 8.8 mm:danio-aesculapii-branching-tree" ;
